cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TCI — The Compute Indices"
message: >-
  If you cite a value, cite the print date, the methodology version and the lock hash
  alongside it, so the claim can be checked rather than trusted. The machine-readable
  equivalents of all three are in site/data/latest.json.
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  A daily, reproducible reference price for renting AI compute delivered from the
  EU/EEA. The headline series TCI-CRI-H100 prices one NVIDIA H100 SXM 80GB GPU-hour,
  on-demand, per-GPU, ex-VAT, as a capacity-weighted median over offers, published with
  its full constituent set. A session below the provider gate is published as a gap and
  is never back-filled or carried forward.
authors:
  - family-names: Rusch
    given-names: Mark
    email: rusch.mh@gmail.com
    city: Amsterdam
    country: NL
repository-code: "https://github.com/markrusch/Compute-Indices"
url: "https://thecomputeindices.com"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - price index
  - reference rate
  - GPU compute
  - benchmark
  - IOSCO
  - reproducible research
# The methodology version, not the Python package version: it is the methodology that
# identifies which construction produced a given print. The -dev suffix is load-bearing
# and means pre-launch, so values may be revised.
version: 0.3.0-dev
date-released: "2026-07-18"
